<div style="max-width:640px;margin:0 auto;padding:80px 24px 40px;">
    <h1 class="cw" style="font-size:32px;margin:0 0 16px;">About this project</h1>
    <p class="fs15" style="opacity:.75;line-height:1.6;">
        This project was scaffolded with <code>lm create</code>. The navigation bar and
        footer you're looking at right now are LumenJS <strong>widgets</strong> — real
        files under <code>src/views/widgets/</code>, wired into
        <code>src/layouts/default.layout</code>. Unlike this page's own content, they
        don't re-render when you navigate between pages.
    </p>
    <p class="fs15" style="opacity:.75;line-height:1.6;">
        Add more pages under <code>src/views/</code>, more widgets under
        <code>src/views/widgets/</code>, and point any layout element at one by giving it
        a bare attribute matching the widget's name — LumenJS mounts and keeps it
        persistent automatically.
    </p>
    <a href="/" class="cw fs14" style="opacity:.85;">Back home</a>
</div>

<settings>
{
    layout: 'default',
    requireAuth: false
}
</settings>
